Conceptual shape of a request:

endpoint:  "https://<provider>/generate"
api_key:   "sk-••••••••••••" (kept secret, never shared publicly)
payload:   {
             prompt: "Summarize this text in one sentence.",
             max_output_length: 50
           }

response:  {
             output: "The text explains how photosynthesis works.",
             tokens_used: 34
           }

Conceptual request — turning a complaint into a one-sentence summary:

endpoint:  ".../generate-text"
api_key:   "sk-••••••••••••"
payload:   {
             prompt: "Summarize this customer complaint in one sentence.",
             input_text: "Delivery was three days late; no response to emails.",
             max_output_length: 40
           }

response:  {
             output: "The delivery was three days late and the customer never got a response.",
             tokens_used: 27
           }

Two providers, two different field names for the same idea:

Provider A response: { output: "Here is your summary." }
Provider B response: { text:   "Here is your summary." }

Same concept, different label — your code has to match whichever field the specific provider actually uses.
